    ("Leaving out pronouns; giving with ให้",
     "When it is clear who or what you mean, Thai simply drops the pronoun: บอกแล้ว = (I) told (him). To give or send something to someone, the order is verb + thing + ให้ (hâi) + person: ส่งลิงก์ให้คุณ = send the link to you. “It” is usually not said at all: พรุ่งนี้จะเอาให้นะ = I'll give it to you tomorrow.",
     [("I'll give it to you tomorrow.", "พรุ่งนี้จะเอาให้นะ", "phrûng-níi jà ao hâi ná"), ("I told him.", "ผมบอกเขาแล้ว", "phǒm bɔ̀ɔk khǎo lɛ́ɛo")]),
